      <div type="clause" n="76.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 76.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="122" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he þonne on þone geonbyrde þe hine slog<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.31"/>, þonne ætfealle sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.12"/> bót þæm godfæder, swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.29"/> ilce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.32"/> swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.30"/> þæt wite þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.33"/> hlaforde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="54" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.54"/> deð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="122" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he þonne on þone geonb...., ætfealle sio bot þæm godfæder, ....m hlaforde ....</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="122" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he ðonne on þone geonbyrde þe hine sloh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.14"/>, ðonne ætfealle sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.15"/> bot ðæm godfæder, swa same<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.6"/> swa þæt wite ðam hlaforde deþ.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="123" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he ðonne on ðone geonbyrde ðe hine sloh, ðonne ætfealle seo bot þam godfǽdere, swa [same<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.5"/>] swa þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite ðam hlaforde deð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="123" ed="#liebermann"/>Si de parentela ipsius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.20"/> sit qui occidit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.21"/> eum, tunc excidat emendatio patrini, sicut manbota<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.22"/> domini.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="60" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he þonne on þone geonbyrde þe hine slog, þonne ætfealle sio bót þæm godfæder<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Ine_76-2.attnote.fn.14"/>, swa ilce<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Ine_76-2.attnote.fn.13"/> swa þæt wite þam hlaforde deð.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="78.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="436" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif he þonne on þone geonbryde þe hine slog, þonne ætfealle sio bot þam godfæder, swa ilce swa þæt wite ðam hlaforde deð.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="123" ed="#liebermann"/>Falls jener jedoch auf denjenigen, der ihn tödtete, losgeschlagen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.de.1"/> hatte, dann entgehe diese Busseneinnahme dem Taufvater ebenso wie jene Strafgeldeinnahme [aus Mannbusse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_76-2.lnote.de.2"/> in solchem Falle] dem Herrn entgeht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if that man had attacked the one who killed him, then let this compensation be lost to the godfather, just as that fine-income [from man-compensation in such a case] is lost to the lord.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="61" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, he was engaged in a struggle with him who slew him, the godfather shall lose his compensation, just as [in similar circumstances] the lord loses his fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="408" ed="#whitelock"/>If, however, he was resisting him who slew him, then the compensation to the godfather is remitted, in the same way as the fine to the lord is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="437" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If [the decedent], however, was resisting in a fight the one who slew him, the compensation to the godfather is nullified, just as is the fine due to the lord.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur (unter welcher einst</hi> ilce?); <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi> same</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure (under which formerly ilce?); in the 16th cent. same</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The note number is printed 5, but the note on [same] is no. 4 (as in 76, 1); no. 5 belongs to ðem in 76, 3.</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius <hi rend="italic">Lond; fehlt Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius Lond; lacking in Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e. o. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e. o. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">123</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">wita</hi> <hi rend="italic">Hn</hi> 79, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">wita</hi> Hn 79, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oh <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oh on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> seo</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to seo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sloh <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sloh So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seo <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seo Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">same <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ld adds same</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ylce <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ylce So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæm <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæm So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.oe.54" n="54" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">122</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rd <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rd So</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The note number is printed 54 in the text, but the note that belongs here is no. 34 (‘-rd So’); there is no note 54 on the page.</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">gebyrede</hi> (‘ad eum pertinebat, ihm zugehörte’) scheint Q irrig im Sinne zu haben. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Notwehr 3; <hi rend="italic">ætfealle</hi> heisst nicht ‘decrease’ (Price), ‘diminution’ (Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi>), sondern ‘falle fort’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q seems mistakenly to have had <hi rend="italic">gebyrede</hi> (‘ad eum pertinebat, belonged to him’) in mind. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Notwehr 3; <hi rend="italic">ætfealle</hi> means not ‘decrease’ (Price) or ‘diminution’ (Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi>), but ‘be lost’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_76-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">wite</hi> heisst öfters ‘Busse’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Strafe 1. Q erklärt richtig ‘Mannbusse’ (ebenso Hn 75, 5 a), behält aber in Hn 79, 1 <hi rend="italic">wita</hi> aus Ags. Orig. bei</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">wite</hi> often means ‘compensation’; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Strafe 1. Q rightly explains it as ‘manbot’ (likewise Hn 75, 5 a), but in Hn 79, 1 keeps <hi rend="italic">wita</hi> from the Anglo-Saxon original</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_76-2.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>ilce</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">same</hi>. H &amp; B*.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 13 is printed 2 times on the page (76.1, 76.2), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_76-2.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>godfæder</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">godfædere</hi>. B.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
